# What git leaves out of the RFind-sc paper repository (reorganised 2026-09-28).
# Policy (2026-09-16; manuscript/ left out since 2026-10-15): publish the code, the fixed inputs and analysis/ (licences: README, "License").
# Left out: raw data that public databases provide, large intermediates that the scripts
# regenerate, personal environment files and the run logs in logs/. GitHub rejects files over 100 MB and warns
# over 50 MB. Keep comments on their own lines: git reads "pattern # text" as one pattern.

# ---- data/ -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Left out: raw downloads (sources in README, "Input data") and pipeline intermediates (data/*/output/: count
# matrices and per-cell signatures, 0.1-0.5 GB each; data/Perturbseq/: pseudo-bulk pb_*.npz, 21-53 MB each and
# 0.3 GB in all, and the stress axes). pb_g151.npz and the group-017 files are not rebuilt by these scripts alone
# (README), so they need a home outside git (e.g. a data archive) if the Perturb-seq steps are to be rerun.
# Tracked: data/*/provided/, the inputs this study supplies: the three fixed inputs of 2026-09-14 (Scrublet
# doublets, De Donno UMAP, CORT table), the Hammond per-cell metadata and mitochondrial fraction (cell_meta_hammond.csv,
# mt_frac_hammond.csv; derived from GEO GSE121654 and the annotated object, the mitochondrial fraction computed from the
# GEO DGE files; analysis/hammond/run_all.sh copies them to data/Hammond2019/raw/), the fixed UMAP of Fig. 1a
# (fig1a_sim_umap_261015.csv), the KA6h reference table (DeDonno_KA6h_deferred.csv, a fixed input of
# analysis/dedonno/03_references.R).
# Also tracked: data/Perturbseq/urls.txt, the list of the atlas's parquet URLs (public) that
# analysis/perturbseq/01b_scan_subclasses.py reads.
# data/GSE169505/ and data/GSE75431/ are the downloads of the two added type A references of Supplementary Fig. S4
# (sources in README, "Input data") and their fold-change tables (fig5_extra_refs.R); not tracked. The reference lists
# themselves are tracked in figs/Fig5_benchmark/output/extra_refs/fig5_extra_refs.rds.
/data/*
!/data/*/
/data/*/*
!/data/*/provided/
!/data/Perturbseq/urls.txt
# the reference lists built by analysis/hammond/06_build_references.R are redistributed (were Reference/output/ until 2026-10-01)
!/data/Hammond2019/output/
/data/Hammond2019/output/*
!/data/Hammond2019/output/references/

# ---- analysis/ (folders reorganised 2026-10-01: pipeline/, quality_control/ and results/ -> analysis/; tidied 2026-10-05) --
# Tracked (small files). analysis/perturbseq/results/ holds the four rankings of Fig. 4 and the two checks quoted in Methods
# (base_check/all_minc5: a lower limit of 5 nuclei; base_check/all_minc10_no_microglia: the GABAergic ranking without the
# microglia-specific genes), written by analysis/perturbseq/03_axis_vs_ko.py with PERTURB_MINC, PERTURB_DROP and PERTURB_RES.
# The reference lists that the pipeline builds are in data/Hammond2019/output/references/; analysis/hammond/data_acquisition/
# keeps the record of how the Hammond input was assembled.

# ---- figs/ -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked: scripts, figures (png, pdf), summary tables (incl. Supp_S2_Delta/output/data/).
# Left out: per-cell scores of the Fig. 5 benchmark and of the
# VISION/Beyondcell check (1-21 MB each) and the knock-out x knock-out RFind scores of Supplementary Fig. S3
# (rfind_allpairs_*.npz, 12-15 MB each); the scripts in figs/*/analysis/ regenerate them.
/figs/*/output/**/*percell*
/figs/Supp_S3_Perturbseq/output/data/*.npz

# ---- logs/ -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# written by the run scripts (run logs, summaries, the Fig. 5 benchmark folders); not tracked
/logs/

# ---- tools/ ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not tracked: clones of the companion packages, which are separate git repositories (github.com/tmurano/RFindsc,
# github.com/tmurano/rfindsc-py); analysis/check_rfindsc.R expects a clone of RFindsc in tools/RFindsc (README).
# rfindsc-py is not needed to run this project: the Python scripts use analysis/running_fisher.py, a copy of its
# Running Fisher kernel.
/tools/RFindsc/
/tools/rfindsc-py/
# Beyondcell v2.2.2 source checkout, used only by the optional 'source' route of figs/Fig5_benchmark/analysis/fig5_bench_redo.R
# (BEYONDCELL_ROUTE; the paper uses the installed package)
/tools/beyondcell_v2.2.2/

# ---- demo/ -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked: the demo data (about 2.7 MB), the scripts and the expected output. Left out: the outputs of a run.
/demo/output_R.csv
/demo/output_py.csv
/demo/output_package_R.csv
/demo/output_package_py.csv

# ---- not code: working notes, slides, documents, papers ------------------------------------------------
# internal hand-over notes between work sessions
/HANDOVER.md
# slides, Word files and the files for the journal
*.pptx
/*.docx
/submission/

# ---- large data formats, wherever they are (safety net) --------------------------------------------------
*.h5ad
*.duckdb
*.npz

# ---- personal environment --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# local tool settings (.claude/, CLAUDE.md), macOS, Office lock files, R, Python
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
.DS_Store
~$*
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rapp.history
.Rproj.user/
Rplots.pdf
*.Rcheck/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# ---- private notes (never published) ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/RFind-sc_private/
